WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.847 --> 00:00:05.259
In the workshop of the plant stands the frame of the filling unit for line 3.

2
00:00:05.936 --> 00:00:08.502
Two uprights and a beam, still loose.

3
00:00:09.518 --> 00:00:12.908
Welding joins metal parts by melting their edges together.

4
00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:15.703
Bolts and glue do it without melting.

5
00:00:16.727 --> 00:00:18.376
Six topics follow the frame.

6
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.828
Three are about welding and what goes wrong in it.

7
00:00:22.879 --> 00:00:26.095
Two are about bolts and glue, joining without melting.

8
00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.229
The last is about welding in production.

9
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.325
The first topic is Arc welding.

10
00:00:33.073 --> 00:00:36.161
A welder joins the corners of the frame, with an arc.

11
00:00:37.241 --> 00:00:39.586
The arc melts the edges of the parts.

12
00:00:40.305 --> 00:00:42.360
The weld pool sets into the weld.

13
00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:45.200
Shielding gas keeps the air away.

14
00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:50.543
For arc welding we often use MIG or MAG, and TIG.

15
00:00:51.838 --> 00:00:53.765
The second topic is Spot welding.

16
00:00:54.491 --> 00:00:57.463
The product will fall through the plate into the cartons.

17
00:00:58.201 --> 00:01:01.069
A guard of two thin sheets keeps hands away there.

18
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.980
A weld gun squeezes the sheets together between

19
00:01:05.014 --> 00:01:07.720
copper electrodes and sends current through.

20
00:01:08.414 --> 00:01:10.179
Where they touch a nugget melts.

21
00:01:11.175 --> 00:01:13.892
For spot welding we often use a tip dresser.

22
00:01:15.212 --> 00:01:18.393
The third topic is Weld defects and inspection.

23
00:01:19.099 --> 00:01:22.582
Before the frame has to carry the unit, we check the welds.

24
00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:27.445
A weld can look perfect outside and hide a gap inside.

25
00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.405
Under load it grows into a crack.

26
00:01:31.432 --> 00:01:36.169
For weld defects we often test with dye penetrant and ultrasonic testing.

27
00:01:37.453 --> 00:01:39.717
The fourth topic is Bolted joints.

28
00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.168
The plate hangs from the beam on four bolts.

29
00:01:43.875 --> 00:01:46.383
That way it can come off again for service.

30
00:01:47.418 --> 00:01:50.483
A bolted joint has a bolt, a nut and a washer.

31
00:01:51.307 --> 00:01:54.639
The property class on the head says how strong the bolt is.

32
00:01:55.698 --> 00:01:57.916
For bolts we often use a nutrunner.

33
00:01:59.246 --> 00:02:02.056
The fifth topic is Bonding and mechanical joining.

34
00:02:02.758 --> 00:02:05.777
The plastic cover goes on the steel frame with glue.

35
00:02:06.755 --> 00:02:10.737
Glue joins plastic to steel without heat and seals out water.

36
00:02:11.507 --> 00:02:13.957
Riveting and clinching join mechanically.

37
00:02:14.941 --> 00:02:17.437
For bonding we often use a static mixer.

38
00:02:18.753 --> 00:02:21.214
The sixth topic is Welding in production.

39
00:02:22.004 --> 00:02:25.696
For a series a robot welds the corners, in a fenced cell.

40
00:02:26.694 --> 00:02:28.540
The parts have to stay in place.

41
00:02:29.264 --> 00:02:31.807
Otherwise the heat of welding warps the frame.

42
00:02:32.783 --> 00:02:36.545
For production we often use a welding fixture and a positioner.

43
00:02:37.606 --> 00:02:40.520
The frame is done, with plate, guard and cover.

44
00:02:41.243 --> 00:02:43.623
It goes to hall B, to line 3.

45
00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.103
This is the whole map.

46
00:02:46.822 --> 00:02:50.456
Welding and joining is the fifth station of Making things.

47
00:02:51.483 --> 00:02:53.178
Every topic has four levels.

48
00:02:54.169 --> 00:02:56.619
Start with Arc welding, at Basics level.

49
00:02:57.337 --> 00:03:00.228
That lesson shows how an arc melts parts together.

50
00:03:01.307 --> 00:03:05.730
At Working knowledge level you set weld parameters and maintain the tips.

51
00:03:06.432 --> 00:03:08.661
You inspect welds, work with torque,

52
00:03:08.835 --> 00:03:11.749
bond in production and choose the welding sequence.

53
00:03:12.742 --> 00:03:16.573
At Advanced level you put welds on paper and check spot welds.

54
00:03:17.289 --> 00:03:20.110
You choose the quality level and the tightening method,

55
00:03:20.261 --> 00:03:22.896
place rivets and work out the cost of a weld.

56
00:03:23.991 --> 00:03:28.565
At Expert level you know what heat does to the steel and read the weld lobe.

57
00:03:29.273 --> 00:03:32.779
You look for recurring defects, design bolted joints,

58
00:03:32.907 --> 00:03:35.450
choose the method and guard weld quality.

59
00:03:36.425 --> 00:03:40.488
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
